=== Governance ===

'''BITCORE retains full control.''' Amendments and writing requests occur in BITHUB.

'''This is not a DAO.''' The V1 branch explicitly rejected the claim that the system distributed governance authority merely because it used networked infrastructure.

== V2 lineage note ==

This branch remains valuable because it preserves several formulations that would otherwise be lost in a canonical merge: ''professional research space, not an authoritative source''; radical realism; evidence as context-dependent; assessment over pedigree; multiple methods of knowing; and the historical BITHUB-mediated authorship model.

